# AI-hint: Defines Git line-ending normalization rules to ensure cross-platform compatibility, specifically enforcing LF for shell scripts to prevent "bad interpreter" errors in containerized environments.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Binaries: never eligible for text normalization. `* text=auto` leaves this to
# content detection, which a tree-wide rewrite can defeat -- eight binaries
# (7z.dll/exe, MiosServiceTool.exe, the branding and portal icons) were once
# committed with their CR bytes stripped, destroying every PE and PNG header.
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.so binary
*.bin binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.xz binary
*.zst binary
*.gguf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
# The legacy archive is a bare git store (ADR-0030 Decision 7): its packs, HEAD and config are
# git's own bytes, which no conversion may touch. On a conflict, re-run `mios-gen archive`.
.archive/** binary
